      "widgets_values": [
        "## The verification loop\n\n`Linear Regression Train` outputs the learned `w` / `b`. The stateless `Linear Regression` node recomputes `y_hat = X·w + b`, and `Squared Loss` compares it against the ground-truth `y` — the verified loss must match the tail of the training loss curve (watch the **loss curve** Plot node on the left).\n\n### Try your own data\n\nWire any labelled `DATASET` (e.g. `Read CSV → Dataset`, or `Formula Data Generator`) into the trainer's **dataset** input — it overrides the synthetic `X` / `y`. Tune `num_steps` / `batch_size` / `lr` on the trainer for your scale."
      ]
    },
